1. REBUILD THE TOP STATUS BAR

Remove permanent Wallet balance from shared NODE-OS chrome.

Wallet balance belongs inside Wallet, not in the OS status bar.

The normal NODE-OS top bar should communicate:

- canonical Firmware identity
- canonical local Device display name
- canonical local IP
- current clock time
- restrained connectivity indication derived from canonical local runtime state

A target presentation is conceptually:

NODE-OS / node-01      198.51.100.23      15:53:14      ●

Exact responsive composition may differ.

Requirements:

- Firmware name comes from localDevice.firmware.name
- Device name comes from localDevice.displayName
- IP comes from localDevice.network.ip
- connectivity comes from localDevice.runtime.networkStatus
- time should display seconds
- no Wallet balance
- no hardcoded NODE-OS or node-01 duplicates as presentation truth
- remove the current boxed `N` brand mark if it no longer fits the mature
  NODE-OS language

The status bar must remain compact and usable at narrow mobile widths.

Do not allow horizontal page overflow.


