3. REPLACE THE CONSUMER-LIKE APP GRID

The Home launcher should become a two-column technical control surface.

Each application remains clearly launchable, but controls should resemble
professional soft keys / system modules rather than consumer app icons.

Each control should use:

- a compact technical icon/glyph area
- application name
- an optional small secondary line
- a large accessible invisible/visible hit target
- restrained technical framing

Visual direction:

┌─────────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐
│ >_  TERMINAL        │  │ ◎   SCAN            │
│     LOCAL SHELL     │  │     KNOWN SPACE     │
└─────────────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘

Use:

- square or near-square geometry
- thin low-contrast borders or technical corner framing
- compact spacing
- restrained green accents
- neutral white/gray structure

Avoid:

- large centered icons
- rounded consumer cards
- large empty card interiors
- glass effects
- glossy panels
- gradients inside controls
- excessive glow
- oversized labels
- decorative activity


